{"version":1,"slug":"Others__General_Awareness_-_General_Studies_-_Super_Practice_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_41738_(20Q)","path":"Others/General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 41738 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 41738 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of a trapezium with bases 37 cm and 29 cm and height 53 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>37 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 29 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 53 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3498 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3498 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2488 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2488 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2864 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2864 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1749 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1749 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>The area of a trapezium = 1/2  X  (sum of bases)  X  height</p><p>= 1/2  X  (37 + 29)  X  53 </p><p>= 1749 cm&#178;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A rectangular park is 60 m long and 40 m wide. A path of uniform width is constructed inside the park along its edges. If the area of the path is 384 m&#178;, find the width of the path.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; 60 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2341; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 384 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1.5 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2.5 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 &#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total area of the park = 60  X  40 = 2400 m&#178;</p><p>Let, x = width of the path</p><p>Then the inner rectangle has dimensions (60  -  2x) m and (40  -  2x) m.</p><p>Area of the inner rectangle = (60  -  2x)(40  -  2x) m&#178;</p><p>Area of the path = Area of outer rectangle  -  Area of inner rectangle = 2400  -  (60  -  2x)(40  -  2x) = 384</p><p>So,</p><p>(60  -  2x)(40  -  2x) = 2400  -  384 = 2016.</p><p>Take x = 2:</p><p>(60  -  2 X 2) = 56, (40  -  2 X 2) = 36 &rarr; 56  X  36 = 2016.</p><p>This satisfies the equation.</p><p>Therefore, x = 2 m</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the perimeter of the square is 64 cm. What is the area of a circle whose radius is half of the side of the square?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 64 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">62&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">62&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Perimeter of square A = 64 cm</p><p>Side of square A = P/4 = 16 cm</p><p>Radius of the circle is = &pi;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of circle = &pi; x 8 x 8 = 64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></p><p></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The length of a rectangular plot is thrice its breadth. If the area of the rectangular plot is 2700 m<sup>2</sup>, then what is the breadth of the rectangular plot?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2349;&#2370;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2349;&#2370;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 2700 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2349;&#2370;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30 m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28 m</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let length and breadth of rectangular plot is '3s' and 's' respectively.</p><p>Area = 3s * s = 2700</p><p>s = 30</p><p>Breadth of the rectangular plot = s = 30 m</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a circle and a square is same. If the radius of the circle is 28 cm, then find the area of the square (in cm<sup>2</sup>).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;/&#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 28 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1936</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1936</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">784</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">784</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1156</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1156</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1369</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1369</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The radius of the circle = 28 cm</p><p>Perimeter of circle = Perimeter of square</p><p>2*22/7 * 28 = 4*side</p><p>Side = 44 cm</p><p>So, the area of the square = 44*44 = 1936 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which will provide more area?</p><p>I. A rectangle of length 4.5 cm and width 2 cm.</p><p>II. A square of perimeter 12 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p>I. &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 4.5 cm &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 2 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>II. 12 cm &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Both will provide equal area</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Cannot be determined</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><b>From statement I:</b></p><p>Area of rectangle = L * W = 4.5 * 2 = 9 sq. cm</p><p><b>From statement II:</b></p><p>Side of square = 12/4 = 3 cm</p><p>Area of square = 3 * 3 = 9 sq. cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a rectangle is 68 cm. If the area of the rectangle is 240 cm<sup>2</sup>, then what is the length of each of its diagonals?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 68 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 240 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">26 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Perimeter of a rectangle = 2(L+B) = 68 cm</p><p>Area of rectangle = LB = 240 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>2[(240/L) + L] = 68</p><p>L = 24 cm and B = 10 cm</p><p>Length of diagonal = &radic;(B<sup>2</sup>+L<sup>2</sup>) =&radic;(10<sup>2</sup>+24<sup>2</sup>) = 26 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Area of a rhombus is 96 cm<sup>2</sup> and length of its one diagonal is 12 cm. Find the length of side of rhombus.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 96 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 12 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Area of rhombus = (1/2) * Product of its diagonal</p><p>96= (1/2) * d<sub>1</sub> * d<sub>2</sub></p><p>192 = 12 * d<sub>2</sub></p><p>d<sub>2</sub> = 16 cm</p><p>Length of side of rhombus = &radic;[(16/2)<sup>2</sup> + (12/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 10 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The length of a rectangle is 2/7<sup>th</sup> of the side of a square and breadth of the rectangle is one-eighth of the side of the square. If the area of the rectangle is 112 m<sup>2</sup>, then what is the perimeter of the square?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 2/7&#2357;&#2366;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 1/8&#2357;&#2366;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 112 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">222 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">222 m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">226 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">226 m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">224 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">224 m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">228 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">228 m</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let side of the square is x m.</p><p>So, length of the rectangle = 2x/7 m and breadth of the rectangle = x/8 m</p><p>2x/7 * x/8 = 112</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> = 56 * 56</p><p>=&gt; x = 56 m</p><p>Hence, perimeter of the square = 4 * 56 = 224 m</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The ratio of the perimeter of a rectangle to the perimeter of a square is 13: 12. If the side of the square is equal to the breadth of the rectangle and the length of the rectangle is 56 cm, then find the breadth of the rectangle. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 13: 12 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;, &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 56 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">48 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">52 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">52 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">44 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">44 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The perimeter of the rectangle/ The perimeter of the square = 13/12 </p><p>[2 (Length + Breadth)]/ [4 * Side] = 13/12 </p><p>(56 + Side)/ 2 * Side = 13/12 </p><p>672 + 12 Side = 26 Side </p><p>14 Side = 672 </p><p>Side = 48 cm </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The length of a rectangle is X times of its breadth. If the breadth of rectangle is 20 cm, then for what value of X, the area of rectangle will be 1000 sq. cm?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; X &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 20 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 1000 sq. cm &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Breadth of rectangle = 20 cm</p><p>Length of rectangle = 20X cm</p><p>Area of rectangle = 1000 sq. cm</p><p>20X * 20 = 1000</p><p>X = 10/4</p><p>X = 5/2</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The circumference of a circle is 100 cm. The side of a square inscribed in this circle is</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 100 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">100&radic;2/&pi; cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100&radic;2/&#960; cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50&radic;2/&pi; cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50&radic;2/&#960; cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100/&pi; cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100/&#960; cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50&radic;2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50&radic;2 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":" <p>Circumference of a circle = 100 cm</p> <p><img width=93 height=86 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/http://188.166.225.173/images/sscimg/8023/image084.png\"></p> <p>Let r be the radius of circle</p> <p>2&pi;r = 100</p> <p>r = 50/&pi;</p><p>AC = diagonal of square = 2r = 100/&pi;</p><p>Hence, side of square = 100/(&pi;&radic;2) = 50&radic;2/&pi; cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the area of rectangle is 4 times the area of square of side '2a' cm. Length of rectangle is 30 cm more than its width that is 'a' cm. Find the value of a (in cm).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354;, '2a' cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; 4 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2360;&#2375; 30 cm &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2396;&#2366;&#2312; 'a' cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; a &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; (cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3/4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3/4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Width of the rectangle = a</p><p>Length of the rectangle = (a + 30) cm</p><p>Area of rectangle = 4 * Area of square</p><p>a * (a + 30) = 4 * (2a)<sup>2</sup></p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + 30a = 16a<sup>2</sup></p><p>15a = 30</p><p>a = 2 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A park ABCD has sides AB and CD parallel to each other. Length of side AB is 10 m and length of side CD is 16 m. If the area of the park is 65 m<sup>2</sup>, what is the perpendicular distance between sides AB and CD?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; ABCD &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AB &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 10 m &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; CD &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 16 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 65 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; AB &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">7m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8m</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>As evident from the question, the park is in the shape of a trapezoid.</p><p>Area of a trapezoid = <img width=401 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20770/image005.png\"></p><p>Distance between sides AB and CD = <img width=89 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20770/image006.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The ratio of length and breadth of a rectangle is 5:3 respectively and breadth of the rectangle is 24% of the side of a square. If the perimeter of the square is 900 cm, then find the area of the rectangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5:3 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 24% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 900 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5600 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5600 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4860 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4860 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3750 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3750 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6050 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6050 cm<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Perimeter of the square = 900 cm</p><p>Side of the square = 900/4 = 225 cm</p><p>Breadth of the rectangle = 24% of 225 = 54 cm</p><p>Length of the rectangle = 54*5/3 = 90 cm</p><p>Area of the rectangle = 90 * 54 = 4860 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The cost of painting a square plate is Rs 5 per m<sup>2</sup>. Find the cost of painting a square plate whose perimeter is numerically equal to its area?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; 5 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs 80</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">80 &#2352;&#2369;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs 40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 &#2352;&#2369;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs 16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2352;&#2369;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs 96</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">96 &#2352;&#2369;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Given, the area = perimeter</p><p>Let side of square be 'x'</p><p> x<sup>2</sup> = 4x or x = 4</p><p> Area = 4*4</p><p>And cost = 4*4*5 = Rs 80</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a square is 1024 sq.m. What is the perimeter of a rectangle whose length is twice the side of the square and the breadth is half the side of the square?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; 1024 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">160 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">160 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">180 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">180 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">200 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">200 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">220 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">220 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let 's' be the side of the square.</p><p>Area of the square = s<sup>2</sup> = 1024 sq m</p><p>s = &radic;1024 = 32 m</p><p>Therefore length of the rectangle = 2*32 = 64 m</p><p>Therefore breadth of the rectangle = (1/2)*32 = 16 m</p><p>Therefore perimeter of the rectangle = 2*(64 + 16) = 160 m.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Base of a triangle is 3/5 times the length of a rectangle. If breadth of the rectangle is 60 cm and area of the triangle is 21/20 of area of the rectangle, then what is the height of the triangle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; 3/5 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354;, &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; 21/20 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">210 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">210 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">240 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">240 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">200 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">200 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">180 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">180 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The area of the triangle is 21/20 of area of the rectangle.</p><p>=&gt; 1/2 * base * height = 21/20 * Length * 60</p><p>=&gt; 1/2 * 3/5 * length * height = 21/20 * length * 60</p><p>=&gt; height = 21 * 3 * 5/3 * 2</p><p>=&gt; height = 210 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Area of a rectangle is equal to the area of rhombus whose diagonals are 16 mm and 40 mm respectively. What is the perimeter of rectangle if its length is 25 mm? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354;, &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 16 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 25 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">68.4 mm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">68.4 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60 mm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72 mm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">75.6 mm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">75.6 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Area of rectangle = Area of rhombus = (1/2) * product of diagonals </p><p>= (1/2) * 16 * 40</p><p>= 320 mm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Then, area of rectangle = length * breadth </p><p>320 = 25 * breadth </p><p>Breadth of rectangle = 12.8 mm </p><p>Therefore, perimeter of rectangle = 2 * (length + breadth)</p><p>= 2 * (25 + 12.8)</p><p>= <b>75.6 mm</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The length and breadth of a rectangle are A cm and B cm respectively. If A: B = 17: 14 and A  -  B = 18, then find the perimeter of rectangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; A cm &#2324;&#2352; B cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A: B = 17: 14 &#2324;&#2352; A - B = 18 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">392 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">392 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">366 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">366 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">344 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">344 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">372 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">372 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let A = 17X and B = 14X</p><p>Given,</p><p>A  -  B = 18</p><p>3X = 18</p><p>X = 6</p><p>So, A = 102 cm, B = 84 cm</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 2 * (A + B) = 2 * (102 + 84) = 372 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}